===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[stop]]-[[motion]]|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|photography}} An [[animation]] technique wherein physical objects are slightly altered and [[photograph]]ed one picture at a time to give an illusion of movement when displayed in sequence.
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=April 26, 2012
|author=Tasha Robinson
|title=Film: Reviews: The Pirates! Band Of Misfits :
|work=The Onion AV Club
|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/the-pirates-band-of-misfits,73064/
|page=
|passage=Jan Švankmajer’s '''stop-motion''' looks angry, rough, and primal; Henry Selick’s is so polished and smooth that it resembles CGI.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[device]] used for automatically stopping a [[machine]] or [[engine]] when a fault or error is detected.<ref>'''stop''', combinations section (''Comb.''), '''stop-motion''' a device for automatically stopping a machine or engine when something has gone wrong (''The New Shorter Oxford English Dictionary'', Clarendon Press, Oxford, Vol. 2 N-Z, 1993 edition, see page 3,074)</ref>

